  "term": "synaptic transmission",
  "definition": "Synaptic transmission is the way a nerve cell sends signals to another neuron, a muscle cell, or a gland cell at a synapse. It may occur chemically through neurotransmitter release and receptor activation in the receiving cell, or electrically through direct ionic current flow across an electrical synapse.",
